					<h2 class="chapter-title" style="margin-top: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Medical &amp; Educational&nbsp;Disclaimer</h2>

					<div class="chapter-content">
						<p style="font-size: 0.98rem; line-height: 1.72; color: #000000; margin-bottom: 1.15rem;">
							<em>Decoding the Burn</em> documents an independent, self-directed citizen research investigation into Burning Mouth Syndrome. The author is a computer programmer and systems researcher, not a licensed medical doctor, dentist, oral surgeon, or neurologist.
						</p>

						<div class="book-callout">
							<span class="book-callout-icon" aria-hidden="true">
								<svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
									<path d="M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z"></path>
									<line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"></line>
									<line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"></line>
								</svg>
							</span>
							<div class="book-callout-text">
								<p style="font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 0.35rem !important;">Important Notice for Readers</p>
								<p style="font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.6; color: #475569;">
									The models, observations, dietary protocols, and tooth margin audits presented in this volume are shared exclusively for educational, investigative, and informational purposes. They are intended to assist patients in framing informed, constructive discussions with qualified clinicians.
								</p>
							</div>
						</div>

						<p style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.7; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
							<strong>1. Not Medical or Dental Advice:</strong> Nothing contained in this book constitutes clinical advice, a medical diagnosis, or a prescribed treatment plan. Burning mouth symptoms can arise from complex systemic pathologies, including autoimmune disorders (such as Sjögren's syndrome), severe nutritional deficiencies (B12, folate, ferritin), contact allergies, fungal infections, or peripheral neuropathies that necessitate comprehensive professional medical evaluation.
						</p>

						<p style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.7; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
							<strong>2. Mandatory Professional Consultation:</strong> Always consult with a qualified, licensed physician, dentist, or oral medicine specialist before adopting, altering, or stopping any diet, nutritional supplement, oral hygiene product, or prescription medication. Never disregard professional clinical judgment or delay seeking medical care because of information read in this&nbsp;guide.
						</p>

						<p style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.7; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
							<strong>3. Individual Variability &amp; Assumption of Risk:</strong> Every human physiology, oral microbiome, and dental architecture is distinct. Applying any elimination protocol, chemical threshold test, or mechanical barrier technique described in this book is undertaken entirely at your own discretion and personal&nbsp;responsibility.
						</p>
