			<!-- PRE-BOOK MENTION: READ BEFORE CHAPTER ONE (Page iv) -->
			<section class="book-page" id="expectation">
				<div class="page-body-content">
					<div class="page-running-head">
						<span class="chapter-header-label">Decoding the Burn</span>
						<span class="page-count-label">Preliminary &bull; Page iv</span>
					</div>

					<h2 class="chapter-title" style="margin-top: 1rem;">Expectations: What You Can Expect from This&nbsp;Book</h2>

					<div class="chapter-content is-first-page">
						<p>Depending on where you are in your journey, you might have high expectations or very low expectations, and both of them are very&nbsp;normal.</p>
						<p>The reality is that every case is different, and this book can only serve or should be viewed as a case study of one person from which you possibly can learn something. You might find ways to reduce your pain, but it is very possible that what I have discovered does not apply to&nbsp;everyone.</p>
						<p>I get what you are going through. I have lived through the acute panic, the sleepless nights, the medical runaround of doctors telling you that everything looks completely fine while your mouth is screaming in fire, and the sheer mental exhaustion of having no clear answers. I have been in those shoes, and I know how deeply isolating this condition&nbsp;feels.</p>
						<p>Early on throughout my BMS journey, I knew that there was some stuff making my pain worse and some stuff making my pain better. So that is the essence of this book: it is not about promising an instant cure or complete healing, but about finding practical ways to minimize the pain at the&nbsp;minimum.</p>
						<p>Sometimes that means changing our daily habits. It means changing what we eat, what we drink, how we brush our teeth, the specialists we seek out, and how we approach dental visits. It might also mean investing in consultations with specific specialists who understand hardware margins, nerve pathways, or tissue biochemistry. I understand that all of this is costly, both financially and emotionally. There is an enormous expenditure of energy, effort, and vulnerability involved, and I completely respect&nbsp;that.</p>
						<p>What I want is to advance the research and share what I have uncovered in the hope that, first, it will directly help some people find relief. And for those for whom my exact findings do not fully work, I hope these observations can serve as the seed for new discoveries that eventually help even the people for whom this initial framework falls short. At the very least, by the time you finish this book, you will have eliminated key variables and gained a much clearer understanding of your personal triggers: what makes your pain better, and what makes it&nbsp;worse.</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="page-number-footer">
					<span>iv</span>
				</div>
			</section>

