					<div id="chapter-3"></div>
					<h2 class="chapter-title">Chapter 3: Why We Need to Do Research: The Hidden Human&nbsp;Toll</h2>

					<div class="chapter-content is-first-page">
						<div id="ch3-work" style="scroll-margin-top: 5rem; margin-bottom: 1.35rem;">
							<h3 style="font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; color: #7c3aed; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">Workplace Struggles</h3>
							<p>Chronic oral burning dismantles daily professional productivity. Whether a sufferer is forced out of the workforce or pushing through intense pain on the job each day because they have to support their family, the toll is immense. Continuous small-fiber sensory firing drains executive bandwidth, generates severe brain fog during meetings, and turns routine communication into an exhausting endurance test.</p>
						</div>

						<div id="ch3-diet" style="scroll-margin-top: 5rem; margin-bottom: 1.35rem;">
							<h3 style="font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; color: #7c3aed; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">Severely Limited Diet</h3>
							<p>Eating ceases to be a source of pleasure and becomes a minefield of physiological triggers. Patients find themselves restricted to a tiny handful of bland, unseasoned foods, forced to eliminate citrus, vinegar, dressings, seasonings, tomatoes, and sauces. Fear of acute flare-ups leads to involuntary weight loss, social dining anxiety, and severe nutritional distress.</p>
						</div>

						<div id="ch3-connection" style="scroll-margin-top: 5rem; margin-bottom: 1.35rem;">
							<h3 style="font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; color: #7c3aed; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">Loss of Connection</h3>
							<p>Living with unrelenting sensory agony alters emotional capacity. When neurological pain monopolizes mental bandwidth 24 hours a day, sufferers frequently experience emotional numbness and a loss of interest in interacting with other people. Relationships with partners, children, and close friends suffer as the ability to share joy or engage socially is consumed by survival.</p>
						</div>

						<div id="ch3-depression" style="scroll-margin-top: 5rem; margin-bottom: 1.35rem;">
							<h3 style="font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; color: #7c3aed; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">Depression and Invalidation</h3>
							<p>Navigating persistent, scalding pain while physical exams appear completely unremarkable creates immense emotional and psychological strain. When standard workups conclude that "everything looks healthy," patients can feel deeply isolated and unheard. Enduring constant physical pain without clear clinical confirmation frequently precipitates situational depression, health anxiety, and profound emotional&nbsp;exhaustion.</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="page-number-footer">
					<span>12</span>
				</div>
			</section>

