						<h4 class="episode-subheading">What Patients Hear When Cleanings Trigger&nbsp;Pain</h4>
						<p>When an ultrasonic cleaning or antimicrobial rinse triggers an unexpected nerve flare, dental professionals naturally evaluate the mouth through standard clinical metrics: checking for calculus, bone loss, or bleeding. Finding none, they offer standard reassurances that, while clinically accurate for periodontal health, leave the patient's burning nerve pain unexplained:</p>
