						<p>Suspecting that acid was penetrating through receding gumlines, I partnered with my dentist to place composite resin bonding patches over exposed cervical root margins. Shielding these open dentinal tubules provided immediate localized relief, reducing baseline pain from 8/10 down to 2-3/10 and confirming that open root dentin acts as a physical conduit transmitting oral acid directly to the dental pulp and trigeminal nerve&nbsp;endings.</p>
