					<h2 class="chapter-title">Chapter 21: Starving the&nbsp;Fire</h2>

					<div class="chapter-content is-first-page">
						<p>When you are in the grip of a 10/10 burning mouth flare, your oral nervous system is caught in an acute electrical storm. You cannot negotiate with the fire, and you cannot test complex&nbsp;multi-ingredient&nbsp;remedies.</p>
						<p>The only way to break the cycle of central sensitization is to cut off 100% of the chemical fuel immediately. This requires an intentional, structured elimination protocol to prove that your symptoms are driven by chemical proton&nbsp;inputs.</p>

						<h3>Protocol 1: The 14-Day No-Acid Elimination Trial (The Absolute Reset)</h3>
						<p>The 14-Day No-Acid Trial is the gold standard diagnostic reset. By eliminating all external dietary acids and 100% of the fermentable carbohydrates that oral bacteria use to manufacture lactic acid, you strip away every chemical trigger simultaneously. The biochemical shift follows a predictable&nbsp;timeline:</p>

						<p><strong>Days 1 to 2 (Starvation of the Biofilm):</strong> External dietary acids stop entering the oral cavity. Without starches or simple sugars, salivary amylase has no substrate to cleave into maltose or glucose. Biofilm bacteria (<em>Streptococcus mutans</em>) are completely starved of fermentable&nbsp;fuel.</p>

						<p><strong>Days 3 to 5 (Extracellular Proton Clearance):</strong> Bacterial lactic, acetic, and propionic acid production collapses toward zero. Gingival sulcus pH rises from an acidic 4.5-5.5 back toward a neutral 7.0-7.4. Free hydrogen protons (H<sup>+</sup>) clear from extracellular fluid, allowing Acid-Sensing Ion Channels (ASIC) and TRPV1 receptors to lock into their closed,&nbsp;resting&nbsp;state.</p>

						<p><strong>Days 6 to 10 (Neural De-escalation):</strong> The continuous volley of high-frequency action potentials traveling up the Trigeminal Nerve subsides. Second-order relay neurons in the brainstem Subnucleus Caudalis drop out of hyperexcitable central&nbsp;sensitization.</p>

						<p><strong>Days 11 to 14 (Deep Baseline Stabilization):</strong> Frayed mucosal tissues enter deep physiological rest. Severe burning scores typically plunge from an agonizing 8-10/10 down to a calm 1-3/10 or complete, quiet&nbsp;silence.</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="page-number-footer">
					<span>52</span>
				</div>
			</section>

