					<div class="chapter-content">
						<h3>What Goes on the Safe Plate (Zero-Acid Baseline)</h3>
						<p>To keep oral pH strictly neutral and deprive bacteria of fermentable fuel, the 14-day zero-acid elimination baseline consists exclusively of clean animal-based whole&nbsp;foods:</p>

						<p><strong>Ruminant Meats:</strong> Ground beef, ribeye, strip steaks, veal, lamb, and nutrient-dense organ meats (liver, heart) providing natural iron, zinc, and bioavailable&nbsp;B-vitamins.</p>

						<p><strong>Poultry and Wild Seafood:</strong> Chicken, turkey, wild salmon, cod, shrimp, and oysters. Naturally neutral in pH and completely free of fermentable&nbsp;carbohydrates.</p>

						<p><strong>Clean Animal Fats:</strong> Beef tallow, suet, duck fat, butter, and ghee for cooking (strictly avoiding seed and vegetable oils that promote systemic&nbsp;inflammation).</p>

						<p><strong>Pasture-Raised Eggs:</strong> Boiled, poached, scrambled, or fried in clean&nbsp;animal&nbsp;fat.</p>

						<p><strong>The Single Whole-Food Plant Exception:</strong> Fresh whole white or cremini mushrooms. Mushrooms possess a neutral pH, virtually zero simple sugars, and structural beta-glucans that oral bacteria cannot ferment into&nbsp;lactic&nbsp;acid.</p>

						<p><strong>Hydration:</strong> Clean, balanced, mineralized spring water (ensuring pH 7.0 to 8.0; avoid unbuffered, acidic reverse-osmosis or distilled water sitting at pH&nbsp;5.5).</p>

						<h3>Immediate Post-Meal Neutralization: The Warm Bicarbonate Protocol</h3>
						<p>Even on an ultra-low-acid baseline, natural meal mastication, salivary shifts, and trace organic compounds can disturb compromised oral surfaces. Standard water merely dilutes surface moisture; it cannot neutralize active protons or restore the missing bicarbonate&nbsp;buffer.</p>

						<p>Establish a mandatory rule immediately following every meal: dissolve half a teaspoon of pure sodium bicarbonate (baking soda) in half a cup of lukewarm water. Swish gently across your tongue, palate, and all gum collars for twenty to thirty seconds. Spit the solution out completely into the sink; do not swallow it. Never follow with cold plain water: allow the alkaline micro-layer to coat your exposed roots and prevent latent bacterial acid&nbsp;fermentation.</p>

						<h3>Seasoning and Sweetener Rules</h3>
						<p>Many patients inadvertently ruin their elimination baseline by overlooking seasonings:</p>
						<p><strong>Eliminate:</strong> Commercial dry rubs, seasoning blends, and marinades. Ingredient labels reveal hidden citric acid, vinegar powders, dextrose, maltodextrin, and onion/garlic powders, all of which rapidly acidify&nbsp;oral&nbsp;tissues.</p>
						<p><strong>Use Only:</strong> Pure mineral salts (Redmond Real Salt, Celtic sea salt) and pure&nbsp;black&nbsp;pepper.</p>
						<p><strong>Sweeteners:</strong> If an intense craving strikes, use only 100% pure stevia extract powder or drops, verifying zero bulking agents like maltodextrin or erythritol that alter osmotic pressure or feed bacterial&nbsp;fermentation.</p>
					</div>
