					<div class="chapter-content">
						<h3>Protocol 2: The 14-Day Low-Acid Dietary Trial (The Gentle Transition)</h3>
						<p>Not every patient can or wishes to jump immediately into a strict zero-carbohydrate carnivore baseline. For flexitarians, vegetarians, or those seeking an approachable plant-modified pathway, the <strong>14-Day Low-Acid Protocol</strong> provides a proven, powerful&nbsp;alternative.</p>
						<p>The principle is straightforward: remove all severe chemical acids and fast-fermenting simple starches, while permitting neutral, non-irritating whole foods that do not depress oral pH below the critical 6.2&nbsp;threshold.</p>

						<h3>Foods Strictly Excluded on the Low-Acid Protocol</h3>
						<p><strong>All Direct Citrus &amp; Sour Fruits:</strong> Lemons, limes, oranges, grapefruits, pineapple, kiwi, and all fruit juices (pH 2.0 to 3.8), which instantly depolarize exposed&nbsp;tubules.</p>
						<p><strong>Vinegars, Pickles, &amp; Ferments:</strong> Apple cider vinegar, balsamic, salad dressings, sauerkraut, and kombucha. Liquid acetic acid bathes nerve terminals directly.</p>
						<p><strong>Tomatoes &amp; Nightshades:</strong> Fresh tomatoes, pasta sauces, salsa, and peppers, carrying natural malic and citric acids alongside inflammatory solanine compounds.</p>
						<p><strong>Coffee, Alcohol, &amp; Carbonated Drinks:</strong> Both regular and decaf coffee sit at an acidic pH 4.8-5.2; sparkling water carries carbonic acid (pH 3.5-4.5); wine and beer deliver potent acid&nbsp;washes.</p>
						<p><strong>The Starch Fermentation Trap:</strong> Commercial breads, crackers, chips, pasta, and pastries. While they do not taste sour, oral bacteria convert them into concentrated lactic acid pools inside gum pockets for 48 to 72&nbsp;hours.</p>

						<h3>Foods Permitted on the Low-Acid Safe List</h3>
						<p><strong>Neutral &amp; Alkaline Vegetables:</strong> Steamed zucchini, peeled cucumbers, fresh white mushrooms, steamed broccoli and cauliflower florets, bok choy, and baby spinach (pH&nbsp;6.5-7.2).</p>
						<p><strong>Clean Proteins:</strong> Skinless chicken breast, roast turkey, baked white fish (cod, halibut), boiled eggs, and unfermented, unsweetened firm tofu.</p>
						<p><strong>Gentle Healthy Fats:</strong> Extra virgin olive oil, fresh avocado slices, grass-fed butter, and ghee, providing essential calories and mucosal lubrication.</p>
						<p><strong>Mandatory Neutralization:</strong> Just like the carnivore reset, the warm sodium bicarbonate rinse after every meal is non-negotiable to neutralize ambient plant acids.</p>
						<p><strong>Expected Outcome:</strong> Most low-acid adherents experience a substantial <strong>40% to 60% reduction in burning intensity</strong> within 10 to 14 days, providing unequivocal proof that oral pain is driven by dietary acidity.</p>
					</div>
