					<div class="chapter-content is-first-page">
						<p>A rigorous first-principles investigation requires accepting that not all burning mouth pain shares the identical origin. While the acid-leak and dentinal tubule pathway explains the sharp sensitivity and flare cycles for a significant subset of sufferers, what happens if eliminating dietary acids brings zero change to your&nbsp;pain?</p>
						<p>If a strict zero-acid baseline and dedicated tubule desensitizers do not shift your daily baseline after 2 to 3 weeks, your burning pain may be driven by primary central neuropathy, autoimmune salivary dysfunction (such as Sjögren's), underlying hematological deficits, or allergic contact sensitivities. In these non-acid cases, there are established clinical interventions and pharmaceutical therapies that have demonstrated measurable relief in peer-reviewed trials and clinical&nbsp;practice.</p>
